jobs.description:
We at EY-Parthenon, a strategic management consultancy hand of EY, are committed to bringing unconventional yet pragmatic thinking together with our clients’ smarts to deliver actionable strategies for real impact in today’s complex business landscape. We develop outstanding leaders who team up to deliver on our promises to all of our stakeholders. In doing so, we play a critical role in building a better working world for our clients, our people and our communities.

As a top tier management consulting company, we serve our clients in multiple industries across multiple project topics, such as Strategy & Growth, Value Creation, Commercial Due Diligence, PMI and many more.

We offer our employees a dynamic working environment with exposure to top-notch regional and international clients and ability to address their strategic challenges and ambitions, while working in a diverse team with great culture and spirit.

Your key responsibilities

As Manager in Corporate Strategy, at EY Parthenon, your will have the following responsibilities:

- Lead client projects and engagement teams to deliver high quality outputs;

- Maintain relationships with client personnel at appropriate levels;

- Drive business development by preparing client meetings and project proposals and proactively seeking and identifying new project opportunities;

- Demonstrate advanced knowledge of all phases and aspects of strategy development and implementation;

- Deliver a high degree of client satisfaction with the engagement process and work products sufficient to drive additional and repeated engagements;

- Develop business strategies using tools such as market analysis, customer research, portfolio optimization, etc;

- Effectively manage diverse and international teams, maintaining the work life balance and promoting EY-Parthenon culture and values;

- Mentor and coach junior colleagues to support their personal and professional growth and fit to the team;

- Lead marketing and promotional efforts to further boost brand presence and awareness;

- Actively support recruitment efforts in identifying and selecting future team members.

Skills and attributes for success

- Able to independently lead projects & teams and manage senior-level clients;

- Highly motivated with positive, “can-do” attitude;

- Team player, capable to effectively operate and communicate in an international, multicultural and diverse environment;

- Strong business acumen and communication skills;

- Proactive and willing to handle several complex tasks simultaneously;

- Outstanding organizational skills, flexibility and ability to work under tight deadlines;

- International exposure and experience (professional and/or educational);

- Capable to effectively contribute and lead business development activities.

To qualify for the role, you must have

- Academic bachelor or master;

- 5-8 years of experience, including in strategic consulting;

- Project management skills: Delivery structure and conclusions, completion of demanding plans, management and coordination of team members and management of the relationship with the client and heads of other departments;

- Commercial skills to identify new customers and opportunities;

- Full Portuguese and English Proficiency;

- Availability to work in Portugal and abroad.

What we offer you

At EY, we’ll develop you with future-focused skills and equip you with world-class experiences. We’ll empower you in a flexible environment, and fuel you and your extraordinary talents in a diverse and inclusive culture of globally connected teams. Learn more.

Are you ready to shape your future with confidence? Apply today.

To help create an equitable and inclusive experience during the recruitment process, please inform us as soon as possible about any disability-related adjustments or accommodations you may need.

EY | Building a better working world

EY is building a better working world by creating new value for clients, people, society and the planet, while building trust in capital markets.

Enabled by data, AI and advanced technology, EY teams help clients shape the future with confidence and develop answers for the most pressing issues of today and tomorrow.

EY teams work across a full spectrum of services in assurance, consulting, tax, strategy and transactions. Fueled by sector insights, a globally connected, multi-disciplinary network and diverse ecosystem partners, EY teams can provide services in more than 150 countries and territories.

At EY, we're committed to providing recruitment and career opportunities to all, regardless of gender, sexual orientation, social background, or disability. We believe that equality and diversity are central to our recruitment process, as they enhance creativity and efficiency, leading to improved performance and productivity. In line with this commitment, EY Portugal recently became a member of the Inclusive Community Forum. This initiative, led by Nova SBE, focuses on the recruitment of individuals with disabilities, advocating for a more inclusive community. Moreover, EY Portugal has also endorsed the Diversity Charter of APPDI (the Portuguese Association for Diversity and Inclusion), pledging to establish and develop internal policies and practices which support diversity. Through these initiatives, EY seeks to actively contribute to the inclusion process, and promote a more inclusive community for people with disabilities, by actively participating in creating solutions.

#LI-HYBRID

EY-Parthenon is a leading global strategy consultancy. We are committed to bringing unconventional yet pragmatic thinking together with our clients, to deliver actionable strategies for real impact in today’s complex business landscape. At EY-Parthenon, we work with corporate and private equity clients to enable them to reinvent themselves for a better future.

The exceptional EY experience. It's yours to build.

The Opportunity: Your Next Adventure Awaits?

EY-Parthenon teams believe every successful business strategy is underpinned by an in-depth understanding of industry dynamics and the competitive landscape in which it sits. EY-Parthenon teams help clients develop actionable and impactful ways to manage complex shifting challenges and transform their organizations.

The team has built an extensive experience in various domains with the value creation spectrum, such as Strategic Transformations, Transaction Strategy and Execution, Commercial Due Diligence, Commercial Strategy & Pricing and Growth Strategies.

EY-Parthenon is a fast-growing service offering within EY Belgium. This is providing new team members broader responsibilities, more exposure to clients and overall, a significant opportunity for personal growth and development. Currently we are looking for a Senior Consultant -Strategy & Transformation to join our team in Belgium.

Key responsibilities

As ‘Senior Consultant’ we expect you to be a clear added value to your project and project manager. You are a go-to-person for (many) junior practitioners. You are able to showcase your topic and/or industry expertise at multiple occasions. Key words in your role are (1) expertise builder, (2) coach & go-to-person, (3) stakeholder manager and (4) challenger.

- TECHNICAL responsibility:

- Delivery excellence: you are able to take responsibility over a project stream (including management of key stakeholders, timelines, important meetings, etc.). You support your project manager on a daily basis and become a ‘wing person’;

- You are fluent in building a story line and in distinguishing key messages from details;

- You can coach up to 3 team members to accelerate their overall development & progress on the project.

- BUSINESS responsibility:

- Sales excellence: you support on ‘Business development’-activities by actively contributing on proposals and driving pieces of it end-to-end based on guidelines and discussions with senior leaders in the firm;

- You support the team in building ‘pitch’ or inspirational documents and join client discussions;

- Building diverse capabilities: you support the market position of EY-Parthenon by driving inspirational eminence pieces forward. You make your community shine by helping out on one or more team activities.

- LEADERSHIP responsibilities:

- Effective communication: you are confident in presenting insights towards senior (client) stakeholders. You have strong stakeholder management skills and are capable in ‘challenging’ your client and leaders in a constructive way;

- Collaboration: you are a go-to-person for both junior practitioners (for coaching) as leaders (for engagement support).

To qualify for the role, you  must have

- A minimum of 2-3 years of working experience in a strategy consulting firm and/or in a corporate strategy departments or strategic roles;

- A Master’s degree in civil/business engineering, economics or similar. An MBA or any additional master’s degree will be considered as a strong asset;

- Strong analytical and problem solving skills with a practical ability to shape the business agenda and define strategic roadmaps;

- Experience with executing complex business projects, working with multi-disciplinary teams;

- Strong internal and external business development acumen;

- An entrepreneurial spirit, team player and excellent communicator;

- Strong affinity with AI & genuine interest in applying new AI trends in a professional context;

- Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, in Dutch, French or English. Preferably you master one of the Belgian national languages.

What working at EY offers

- Attractive remuneration package - we offer an attractive remuneration package; including a company car and fuel/charging card, iPhone plus subscription, health insurance, pension plan, meal vouchers and eco vouchers. We offer a flexible package to our people that gives them the power to choose what they value most; extra days off, leasing an electric bike, etc.

- Inspiring work environment - at EY we are dedicated to providing you with an inspiring work environment. A work environment which allows you to further develop your skills and enables you to fulfill your true potential.

- Personal growth - you will receive numerous trainings and will be coached by a counselor. We offer a clear career path tailored to your unique skills.

- Fun - by joining our EY- teams, you can participate in team activities, family days, summer and winter events, sports events and enjoy a drink during our monthly Together Thursday happy hour.

- Sustainability - we have a fleet of hybrid and electric cars. Our flex plan makes it possible for people that don’t want a company car to choose an even more sustainable option.

- Artificial Intelligence – stay up to date with the latest AI trends through our extensive training opportunities and integrated AI systems. You’ll learn how to leverage AI in a smart and efficient way in your day-to-day work, while developing skills to identify, quantify and track value creation when integrating AI into client environments.

- Diversity & Inclusion - at EY we are passionate about the inclusion and support of individuals of all groups; we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, or disability status.

Join us in building a better working world.

Apply now!

